<article class="env-definition" id="0FFP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FFP">Definition <span data-tag="0FFP">4.43.8</span>.</a> Given a monoidal category $(\mathcal{C}, \otimes , \phi )$ and an object $X$ a <em>left dual</em> is an object $Y$ together with morphisms $\eta : \mathbf{1} \to X \otimes Y$ and $\epsilon : Y \otimes X \to \mathbf{1}$ such that the diagrams </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \vcenter { \xymatrix{ X \ar[rd]_1 \ar[r]_-{\eta \otimes 1} &  X \otimes Y \otimes X \ar[d]^{1 \otimes \epsilon } \\  &  X } } \quad \text{and}\quad \vcenter { \xymatrix{ Y \ar[rd]_1 \ar[r]_-{1 \otimes \eta } &  Y \otimes X \otimes Y \ar[d]^{\epsilon \otimes 1} \\  &  Y } }  \]
</div>
  <p> commute. In this situation we say that $X$ is a <em>right dual</em> of $Y$. </p>
</article>